  "question": {
    "text": "A particle of charge $16 \\times 10^{-16} \\mathrm{C}$ moving with velocity $10 \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}$ along $x$-axis enters a region where magnetic field of induction\n$\\vec{B}$ is along the $y$-axis and an electric field of magnitude $10^4 \\mathrm{Vm}^{-1}$ is along the negative $z$-axis.\nIf the charged particle continues moving along $x$-axis, the magnitude of $\\vec{B}$ is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "aKMzH",
      "text": "\n$16 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~Wb} \\mathrm{~m}^{-2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "p6uFJ",
      "text": "\n$2 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~Wb} \\mathrm{~m}^{-2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "wDwoD",
      "text": "\n$1 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~Wb} \\mathrm{~m}^{-2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "WMcUv",
      "text": "\n$4 \\times 10^3 \\mathrm{~Wb} \\mathrm{~m}^{-2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Since particle is moving undeflected\nSo, $q_E=q v B$\n$$\n\\Rightarrow B=\\frac{E}{V}=\\frac{10^4}{10}=10^3 \\mathrm{wb} / \\mathrm{m}^2\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
